The goal at the moment is to cover only these two (by POCing Java agent instrumentation):

```
java.net.SocketPermission
java.io.FilePermission
```

@reporter cc @participant5 
systemd operates at the service level, while a Java agent operates at the plugin level—this is the fundamental difference. The reason we need to maintain compatibility with SecurityManager is to address isolation concerns for custom plugins. This is because, in the Elasticsearch platform, built-in plugins are trusted, whereas custom plugins are uploaded by users and pose uncontrolled risks.
On the other hand, Elasticsearch 8 introduced entitlements, which already cover most of the functionality previously provided by SecurityManager.
